<title>SWEDEN: Orrefors Kosta Boda jumps as trade resumes.</title>
<headline>Orrefors Kosta Boda jumps as trade resumes.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Swedish glassmaker Orrefors Kosta Boda opened 11 crowns higher at 151 crowns when trading resumed on the Stockholm bourse after news of a takeover bid.</p>
<p>Trading in the luxury glassmaker was suspended on Friday when the company's three key shareholders announced they were in talks over future ownership.</p>
<p>It was last traded at 140 crowns.</p>
<p>The takeover bid by Swedish investment group Proventus AB, Denmark's Royal Copenhagen and Scandinavian Equity Partners Ltd - a Swedish/U.S. investment company - was announced on Tuesday, offering 155 crowns a share.</p>
<p>The largest shareholder, Swedish investment group Investor AB, said it was positive about the bid and was going to sell its 23.1 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
